<section class="page" id="foreword">
  <h2 class="page-title">FOREWORD</h2>
  <div class="panel bg-blue halftone" style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6">
    <p>"Saurāṣṭre somanāthaṃ ca, śrīśaile mallikārjunam…" Many of us learnt these lines as children: a short prayer that is really a map, naming twelve holy places of Śiva from the shore of Gujarat to the snows of Kedār, from Kāśī to the tip of India at Rāmeśvaram.</p>
    <p>The <b>jyotirliṅgas</b>, "liṅgas of light", are the places where Śiva is believed to have shown himself as a column of light. For centuries pilgrims have tried to visit all twelve in a lifetime. The stotram promises that even naming them, morning and evening, carries their blessing.</p>
    <p>This article explains the hymn verse by verse and puts all twelve on one map. Each temple has its own full guide in this series. May every reader see all twelve lights, on the road or in the heart.</p>
    <p style="text-align:right;margin-top:14px"><span class="bang" style="font-size:22px;color:#1d4f9a">Har Har Mahādev,</span><br><span class="bang" style="font-size:26px">srini.presents</span> 🙏</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="page" id="full">
  <h2 class="page-title">THE STOTRAM</h2>
  <div class="sub">Four short verses, for chanting in one go</div>
  <div class="full big" style="font-size:22px"><p><span class="ln">saurāṣṭre somanāthaṃ ca</span><span class="ln">śrīśaile mallikārjunam</span><span class="ln">ujjayinyāṃ mahākālam</span><span class="ln">oṃkāram amaleśvaram</span><span class="ln">paralyāṃ vaidyanāthaṃ ca</span><span class="ln">ḍākinyāṃ bhīmaśaṅkaram</span><span class="ln">setubandhe tu rāmeśaṃ</span><span class="ln">nāgeśaṃ dārukāvane</span><span class="ln">vārāṇasyāṃ tu viśveśaṃ</span><span class="ln">tryambakaṃ gautamītaṭe</span><span class="ln">himālaye tu kedāraṃ</span><span class="ln">ghuśmeśaṃ ca śivālaye</span></p><p style="margin-top:10px"><span class="ln">etāni jyotirliṅgāni</span><span class="ln">sāyaṃ prātaḥ paṭhen naraḥ</span><span class="ln">saptajanmakṛtaṃ pāpaṃ</span><span class="ln">smaraṇena vinaśyati</span></p></div>
  <div class="panel" style="margin-top:12px"><span class="caption">In one line</span><p style="margin:0;font-size:16px">Somanātha, Mallikārjuna, Mahākāla, Oṃkāreśvara, Vaidyanātha, Bhīmaśaṅkara, Rāmeśvara, Nāgeśvara, Viśvanātha, Tryambakeśvara, Kedāranātha, Ghṛṣṇeśvara: <b>name them morning and evening, and the wrongs of seven lifetimes fall away.</b></p></div>
</section>

